# Delivered asset packs: keep the extracted PNGs, not the archives
*.zip

# examples/coup/saturn/cd/*.BIN are deliberately TRACKED, not ignored.
# They are the streamed scene backgrounds. The Docker build copies them onto
# the disc image but cannot regenerate them - convert_backgrounds.py needs
# Python and Pillow, which the hermetic Saturn image does not carry. Ignoring
# them would make a fresh clone build a disc whose every background is black,
# with no build-time symptom. 505 KB total.
#
# This used to be only a comment, and the exemption existed solely because
# someone had run `git add -f` on the files that existed at the time. It did
# not cover new ones: BGSPLASH.BIN was authored, referenced by
# coup_bg_index.h, and shipped on the v2.0-beta disc while never entering the
# repo - and `git status` stayed clean, because the file was ignored. The
# rules below make the exemption real.
#
# The directory must be re-included FIRST: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation for files inside `cd/` is never even
# considered until `cd/` itself is un-excluded. These also override the
# `*.bin` rule above, which matches `.BIN` on case-insensitive filesystems.
#
# Enforced by scripts/qa/qa_disc_assets_tracked.py.
!examples/coup/saturn/cd/
!examples/coup/saturn/cd/*.BIN

# QA captures and build logs - regenerate with scripts/qa/capture_all_screens.sh
build/qa/*.log
